  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "05. Attack Sequence",
    "ruleNumber": "05.01",
    "summary": "Each attack die gets its own D6 hit roll. Every roll is compared with a four-row table, top to bottom, and the first row that fits decides it: an unmodified 1 fails, an unmodified 6 is a critical hit, a result that meets or beats the BS or WS in play scores a hit, and anything else fails.",
